  "material_learning": "A fixed unlevered volatility budget can reduce BTC path risk, but the return cost is regime dependent. In 2020-2022 Design it cut maximum drawdown by 14.43993330 percentage points yet captured only 43.943628 percent of passive upside, leaving Calmar at 0.90762825 versus 1.67905405. The same rule worked much better in 2023-2024, capturing 87.129784 percent of passive upside while reducing drawdown by 6.61836584 percentage points. Only two of five annual folds reached 75 percent of passive Calmar. This instability means recent Validation strength cannot support a candidate.",
